    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;15.04</strong> Favourable subtypes of carcinoma of unknown primary (CUP)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Anthony J. Gill",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 90.38%; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"90%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical and pathological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Subtype of CUP</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Single metastatic deposit or oligometastatic disease amenable to local ablative treatment</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Single-site or oligometastatic CUP<sup>a</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Female patient with isolated axillary lymph node metastases</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Breast-like CUP</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Female patient with peritoneal carcinomatosis of a serous papillary adenocarcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Ovary-like CUP</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Squamous cell carcinoma involving non-supraclavicular cervical lymph nodes</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Head and neck&ndash;like CUP</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Male patient with blastic bone metastases and/or immunohistochemistry or serum PSA expression</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Prostate-like CUP</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Adenocarcinoma with colorectal immunohistochemistry (CK7-negative, CK20-positive, CDX2-positive) or molecular profile</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Colon-like CUP</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.66%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"69%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Carcinoma with renal cell histological and immunohistochemical profile</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.34%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"30%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210074048;\">Renal-like CUP</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>The group of single-site or oligometastatic CUP includes the previously recognized subtype squamous cell carcinoma with inguinal lymph nodes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: The previously recognized poorly differentiated carcinoma with midline distribution (germ cell tumour&ndash;like CUP) is no longer recognized as a subtype of CUP. The previously recognized favourable neuroendocrine carcinoma (NEC) subtype is no longer recognized and should be classified and treated according to guidelines for neuroendocrine malignancies. Adapted from <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{36563965}</span>.</p>",
