    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Carcinoma of unknown primary site reclassified as cholangiocarcinoma after molecular testing",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A</strong>) This patient presented with widespread liver, lung, and bone metastatic disease without any known primary and was initially considered to have carcinoma of unknown primary. Comprehensive genomic testing demonstrated <em>FGFR2</em>::<em>BICC1</em> fusion. In light of this, the morphology was reviewed and thought to be consistent with intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma of small duct type.",
    "source": "Anthony J. Gill",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
